   </p>
   <p class="step" id="step-40" style="display: none;">
                      <!-- "step-40" -->
Some quick math.
<br><br>
There are ten digits 0-9 ; each digit is 10% or .10.
<br><br>
All the even digits count as 5 things.  So , 5 * .10 = .50.
<br><br>
Count 5 as one digit , 1 * .10 = .1.
<br><br>
What is left , 4 digits , 4 * .10 = .4. 
<br><br>
But , 1/3 are going to be eliminated , so .3333 * .4 = .13332.
<br><br>
Next , summing the np (non prime) .5 + .1 + .13332 = 0.73332. 
<br><br>
So , 1 - 0.73332 = 0.26668. 
<br><br>
Therefore ,  26.668% of the *wildcard numbers are ps (prime suspects). 
<br><br>
Finally , looking at the chart on screen page 46 and 48 ; 8 / 30 = 0.2666666.
<br><br>
Roughly 26.66% of all numbers <span style="background-color: lightgrey;">
<u><strong>could</strong></u></span> be a ps (prime suspect).
<br><br>
To a classically trained mathematician this probably math heresy. But in the real world it is close enough. 
<br><br>
<br><br>
<br><br>
<br><br>
<br><br>
   </p>
